  <text xml:lang="ta" type="edition">
    <body>

        <div xml:id="AN257.1-kilavi">
          <p type="edition">uṭaṉpōkāniṉṟa talaimakaṭkut talaimakaṉ colliyatu.</p>
          <p type="translation" xml:lang="en">What HE said to HER when they were going away together.</p>
        </div>
        <div rend="parallel">
      <lg xml:id="AN257.1">
        <l>vēṉiṟ pātirik kūṉi māmalar</l>
        <l>naraivāy vāṭa ṉāṟu nāṭcura</l>
        <l>mariyār cilampiṟ cīṟaṭi civappa</l>
        <l>vemmō ṭōrāṟu paṭīiyar yāḻaniṉ</l>
        <l>pomma lōti potuḷa vāri</l>
        <l><supplied>ya</supplied>rumpaṟa malarnta vāypū marāattuc</l>
        <l>curumpucū ḻa<supplied>la</supplied>ri taii vēyntaniṉ</l>
        <l>ṟēmpāy kūntaṟ kuṟumpala <supplied>mo</supplied>cikkum</l>
        <l>vaṇṭukaṭin tōmpa ṟēṟṟā yaḷikoḷa</l>
        <l>nuṇkō lelvaḷai teḷirkku muṉkai</l>
        <l>melliṟaip paṇaittōḷ viḷaṅka vīci</l>
        <l><supplied>va</supplied>lluvai maṉṉā ṉaṭaiyē kaḷvar </l>
        <l>pakaimiku kavalaic ceṉṉeṟi kāṇmār</l>
        <l>micaimarañ cērttiya kavaimuṟi yāattu</l>
        <l>nārarai maruṅki ṉīrvarap poḻittuk</l>
        <l>kaḷiṟucuvait tiṭṭa kōtuṭait tataral</l>
        <l>kallā vumaṇarkkut tīmūṭ ṭākun</l>
        <l>tuṉpuṟu takuvaṉa vāṅkaṭ paṉkōṭ</l>
        <l>ṭarilivar puṟṟat talkirai nacaii</l>
        <l>veḷḷarā <supplied>mi</supplied>ḷira vāṅkum</l>
        <l>piḷḷai yeṇkiṉ malaivayi ṉāṉē.</l>
      </lg>
      <lg type="translation" xml:lang="en">
        <l>In summer, on a fragrant day of the withering of the grey</l>
        <l corresp="1f">openings on the hunchbacked large blossoms of the trumpet tree, in the desert</l>
        <l corresp="3">so that [your] little feet with anklets in which metal pieces tinkle become red,</l>
        <l corresp="4">may you experience one path with us.</l>
        <l corresp="9">You who do not [even] ensure, with care, to protect [yourself] by chasing away the bees</l>
        <l corresp="8">that swarm, small [and] many, [around] your nectar-flowing tresses</l>
        <l corresp="7">that are covered intricately with the bee-surrounded blossoms</l>
        <l corresp="6">of the Kadamba tree with choice flowers that bloomed without buds,</l>
        <l corresp="5">having fully combed your thick hair,</l>
        <l>flinging your forearms on which fine beautiful bright bangles sparkle</l>
        <l corresp="6f">so that [your] bamboo shoulders with delicate joints shine</l>
        <l corresp="12a-c">yes, you are capable of walking,</l>
        <l corresp="21">- in the mountains of bears [that have] cubs,</l>
        <l corresp="19">who, longing for the anthill that is overgrown by a thicket as [their] night’s prey,</l>
        <l corresp="20">drag away the white snake so that it writhes,</l>
        <l corresp="18">[mountains] with many peaks there, that are fit to undergo misery on,</l>
        <l corresp="16">where the remaining crushed [pieces] tasted [and] put down by the elephant bull</l>
        <l corresp="15">of the [branches] on the ridge so that water came from the side of the bark[-covered] trunk</l>
        <l corresp="12d 14">of the Yām tree with forking shoots that robbers appropriate, as a tree of height,</l>
        <l corresp="13">in order to see the path that goes to inimical crossroads,</l>
        <l corresp="17">becomes the kindling for the fire of the unlearned salt merchants.</l>
      </lg>
        </div>
    </body>
  </text>

